ow inherits it.\n\nThe reachability engine is `tests/closure.py affected`, the gate's own measured\nderivation, run once per invocation (steps 3a/3f3/3f5 share the plan; nothing\nis cached across invocations). A step skips only when the three-dot diff\nintersects nothing in its read-set: the measured closure of every script the\nstep drives that the table records, plus a declared path list where no closure\nexists. Every skip prints prepr's `say skip` line with its disjointness; a\nsilent skip is the defect class this programme refuses.\n\nWhat is skipped, and on what evidence:\n- `mutants` (3a): declared list covering policy_lint_mutants.mjs's reads (its\n  own directory, the POLICY_GLOBS corpus, the corpus READMEs).\n- `field coverage` (3f3): declared list (.claude/, .github/, tools/policy/,\n  tools/release/, round6, dev/governance/) plus the MEASURED closure of\n  `tests/structure.py`, which the step spawns.\n- `register check` (3f5): declared list (dev/audit/ config, rounds, rca).\n\nFail-open at every boundary, never fail-closed to skipping: an unreadable diff,\na failed derivation, a diff `closure.py affected` cannot scope (a changed gate\nfile, or any file no measured table knows), and a diff touching any script the\nclosure table itself measures all run every heavy step exactly as before.\n\nHONEST DISCLOSURE -- what is NOT skipped. The agreement lane (3f4) is left\nunconditional: `agreement_py.py` reads the branch's OWN merge-subject history\n(`git log --first-parent` since the tag through HEAD), so every branch that\nadds a commit provably reaches it and no file table can call that read inert.\nAnd the three provable steps skip only on a diff whose every file the closure\ntable maps: this pull request's own diff touches `tools/pr/prepr.sh`, which no\nmeasured table lists, so all three heavy steps ran on this very branch.\n\nMeasured on a row-only fixture (commit 7f62a36cf, one delivery row over\n81acae2b7), same box, sequential runs, `/usr/bin/time -p`, n